<div class="govuk-grid-row"><div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Site allocations</h1>
<p class="govuk-body-l">A local plan allocates the sites that will deliver its development. This page sets out what the law and national policy ask of those allocations, the four-stage site selection process in the government's guidance, the evidence an Inspector will expect, where sites come up in the 30 months, and the mistakes the guidance warns against.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">Every statement links to the passage it comes from. Work through the <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ rel('/checklists/site-allocations/') }}">site allocations checklist</a> as you go, or <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ rel('/ask/') }}">ask a question</a> about your own sites.</p>

<nav aria-labelledby="contents-heading">
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-s" id="contents-heading">Contents</h2>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li><a class="govuk-link" href="#what-the-law-requires">What the law and national policy require</a></li>
